## 7. HTML Pages — Required Set

### 7a. `index.html` (subproject hub)

Must include:
- Kicker: `<Basin> · <Type> System`
- Title with type badge (`Natural` / `Human`) and paired badge if applicable
- Subtitle: one paragraph with key volumes and paired context
- KPI strip: 4 cards with the most significant quantitative values
- Alert panel: the key structural issue (bottleneck, opacity gap, D-C imbalance)
- Paired panel: link to the natural or human counterpart, with stock ratio or efficiency note
- Three cards: Supply Chain, System Lifecycle, Value Chain (with sub-links to dashboard and sub-pages)
- Navigation: back to basin hub, to paired subproject, to main homepage

Color scheme: use `project.yaml` `ndc_colors` values throughout.

### 7b. `supply_chain/index.html`

Summary page listing the three supply chain sub-pages. Must describe the chain average balance and the bottleneck phase in the subtitle.

### 7c. `supply_chain/dashboard.html`

Dark-themed analytics dashboard. Must include:
- Chain summary KPIs (avg balance, avg N, phase count)
- Bottleneck alert bar (auto-populated from data)
- Phase D-C-N balance bars (loaded from `_supply_chain_ui.json`)
- Five-model coherence pentagon (loaded from `scenarios.json` or hardcoded fallback)
- Phase detail table with transparency badges
- Bottleneck alert text must explain the structural cause, not just name the phase

Colors: pentagon fill from `project.yaml` primary color. Dark theme (`#0d1117` body, `#161b22` panels).

### 7d. `supply_chain/project_context.html`

Light-themed context page. Must include:
- System overview KPI strip
- Supply chain phases table with transparency badges and balance scores
- At least one country-level breakdown table (use metrics CSV data)
- Bond opportunity analysis section (performance trigger, use of proceeds, measurement basis, revenue basis, indicative scale)
- Risk factors table
- Data sources list with URLs

### 7e. `supply_chain/system_lifecycle.html`

Dark-themed lifecycle page. Loaded from `_system_lifecycle_ndc.json`. Must include:
- Summary KPI grid (avg balance, avg N, bottleneck phase, strongest phase)
- Phase lifecycle N-D-C bars for each phase (auto-populated from JSON)
- Infrastructure lifecycle interpretation (3 paragraphs: structure, bottleneck, bond intervention logic)

Bottleneck threshold: phases below 85% balance are flagged as bottlenecks.

### 7f. `value_chain/index.html`

Light-themed value chain overview. Must include:
- e-layer score prominently displayed
- Revenue and cost structure table
- Bond structure table (type, use of proceeds, performance KPI, measurement basis, revenue basis, tenor, eligible issuers, indicative scale)
- Five-model value context table (all 5 axes with score and interpretation for value chain implications)
- Note: if e-layer score is 0 (unmeasured), explain why and what would be needed to activate the financial abstraction layer

---

## 8. Paired Hub Page (`paired_<name>/index.html`)

The paired hub page does NOT have its own PDI, supply chain, or value chain pages. It is a composite view only.

Must include:
- Composite index score (weighted blend of natural and human component balances)
- Interactive weighting slider (natural vs. human)
- Bond grade derived from composite score
- Two component cards showing phase bars for both contributing subprojects
- Links to both contributing subprojects
- Blended coherence summary (recalculated on slider change)

Bond rating thresholds (composite balance score):

| Score | Grade |
|---|---|
| ≥95% | AAA |
| ≥90% | AA+ |
| ≥86% | AA |
| ≥82% | AA- |
| ≥78% | A+ |
| ≥74% | A |
| ≥70% | A- |
| ≥65% | BBB+ |
| ≥60% | BBB |
| <60% | BBB- |

---

## 9. Composite Index Page (basin-level)

The basin hub has one composite index page (`composite_water_index.html` or equivalent) that blends all active subprojects.

When adding a new subproject, update the composite index to:
1. Add the new contributing index data object (balance + coherence + phases)
2. Add a third (or additional) weight slider, normalised to 100%
3. Update the contributing card grid (one card per index)
4. Update the phase comparison table (add a column per new index)
5. Update the bond analysis table (add a row for the new sector)
6. Recalculate the default composite score and bond grade in the hub page card

Default weighting guidance:
- Natural systems: lower weight (covenant/monitoring layer, slow-moving)
- Human systems with regulatory anchor (drinking water): higher weight
- Human systems with efficiency gap (irrigation, navigation): medium weight

---

## 10. Basin Hub Page Updates

When a subproject is fully built, update `frontend/project/<basin>/index.html`:

1. Add a new "Active Pilot" section (matching the freshwater pair or agricultural water pair pattern)
2. In the "Full System Map" section, change the relevant card from `class="coming-card"` to `class="coming-card active"` (for natural/human) or `class="coming-card active-paired"` (for paired)
3. Update the card label from `"<Type>"` to `"<Type> ✓ Active"`
4. Update the composite index card to show the new default score and bond grade

The `active` and `active-paired` CSS classes provide green/orange visual distinction for deployed vs. placeholder cards. Do not mark a card active if the page still shows "Not yet available."

---

## 11. Checklist Before Marking a Subproject Complete

- [ ] `project.yaml` exists with all required fields
- [ ] PDI YAML exists with all 5 phases populated (no OPAQUE phases without explanation)
- [ ] `ndc_derivation` values in PDI match the values in `generate_danube_data.py` `NDC_DATA`
- [ ] Both CSV schema files exist with at least one row per phase in metrics CSV
- [ ] All three JSON files generated successfully (supply_chain_ui, system_lifecycle_ndc, scenarios)
- [ ] All 6 HTML pages exist (index, supply_chain/index, dashboard, project_context, system_lifecycle, value_chain/index)
- [ ] Dashboard loads JSON data correctly (no "Loading..." states left in browser)
- [ ] Bottleneck alert displays the correct phase name and cause
- [ ] Bond opportunity analysis in project_context.html cites real data sources
- [ ] Paired panel on index.html links to the correct counterpart
- [ ] Basin hub index.html has the Active Pilot section for this subproject pair
- [ ] System map card updated to `active` class
- [ ] Composite index updated to include this subproject
- [ ] No em-dashes anywhere in any file (use commas, colons, or separate sentences)
- [ ] `color-scheme: light` declared in all light-themed pages to prevent browser dark mode override

